{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (Phase 1 complete — rebar-debug). CONFIRMED root cause, single mechanism.\n\nMechanism: The provider-parity tests drive the REAL production Bedrock path\n(build_bedrock_provider @ src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py:152), which constructs\n`boto3.session.Session(region_name=region)`. boto3 Session construction eagerly\nresolves the ambient AWS profile via botocore, honoring $AWS_PROFILE and reading it\nfrom the operator's real ~/.aws/config (default AWS_CONFIG_FILE). The test helper\n`_capture` (tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py:634-637) injects dummy\nAWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/SECRET and a region, but does NOT isolate the profile/config-FILE\nresolution. So on a dev box with AWS_PROFILE=frontier + a matching [profile frontier]\nin ~/.aws/config the Session builds and `.converse` is captured (29 pass); under an\nempty/arbitrary HOME the named profile is absent and Session construction raises\nbotocore.exceptions.ProfileNotFound BEFORE `converse`, so no payload is captured and\nthe 6 listed tests fail with \"no outbound request captured for 'bedrock:...'\".\n\nDiscriminating proof (runtime):\n- real HOME: 29 passed. empty HOME: 6 failed / 23 passed (reproduced).\n- Surfaced exception under empty HOME: ProfileNotFound: config profile (frontier)\n  from boto3.session.Session.__init__ -> botocore get_scoped_config.\n- Redirect AWS_CONFIG_FILE/AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE to injected empty files AND\n  DELETE AWS_PROFILE/AWS_DEFAULT_PROFILE under empty HOME -> 29 passed. This isolates\n  ONLY the AWS profile/config-file read (not $HOME, not ~/.gitconfig identity), the\n  DIFFERENT seam this ticket calls for vs frousy's MCP-scanner default-home seam.\n- Negative control: setting AWS_PROFILE=\"\" (present-but-empty) still fails (profile\n  named \"\") — proving the read is specifically profile-NAME resolution against the\n  config-file location, ruling out env-credential/region as the cause.\n\nLegitimacy: defect (test-hermeticity). Authoritative contract: the unit tier's\n\"never touch the real environment\" invariant, embodied in the existing autouse\nconftest fixtures `_no_real_session_log_writes` and `_isolated_mcp_client_home`, plus\nthis ticket's acceptance criteria. Production provider behavior is CORRECT (reading\nAWS_PROFILE is how AWS auth works) and is NOT changed — the fix is test-only.\n\nDefect origin (caused_by): 0d76-ebbf-ee3a-48ac (musical-followable-mouflon, \"S6 —\nclear the parity bar for Bedrock\"), via introducing commit 07d19c5537e1 (\"0d76: prove\npayload and tool parity\"), which added `_capture` and asserted the suite \"stays\noffline and credential-free\" while omitting AWS profile/config isolation. The\nnon-hermeticity has existed since introduction (git blame: 2026-08-02) with no\ngood->bad transition, so 0d76 is the origin, not a carrier or an unmet obligation.\nClass: plan_defect.\n\nFix (Phase 2): a tier-wide autouse conftest fixture in tests/unit/conftest.py that\nredirects AWS_CONFIG_FILE/AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE to an injected empty per-session\ndir and neutralizes AWS_PROFILE/AWS_DEFAULT_PROFILE — mirroring _isolated_mcp_client_home,\nisolating only the credential/config read, leaving $HOME and git identity untouched."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787947575221759001,"uuid":"dfec78f8-fd96-465c-b507-8898ad3640bc"}